<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Imre Thököly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1657">1657</a>–<a href="/years/1705">1705</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Imre Thököly was a Hungarian Lutheran noble who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuruc">Kuruc</a> rebellion against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule from 1678. With Ottoman backing he ruled the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-hungary">Upper Hungary</a> from 1682 and married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilona-zrinyi">Ilona Zrínyi</a>. After the Ottoman defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1683 his state collapsed, and he died in exile in Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/imre-thokoly.jpg" alt="Imre Thököly" width="296" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thokolyi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
